/***********************************************************************************************************************
da4_gethandlersourcehistorypage.probesql -- dbo.uspGetHandlerSourceHistoryPage (script 504).

Run: sqlcmd -S localhost -E -C -I -d RCRAInfo -y 0 -i "C:\~MDE-55TT2J4\RCRAInfo\build\tmp\da4_gethandlersourcehistorypage.probesql"
-I is REQUIRED. dbo.HandlerSource carries a filtered unique index (UX_dbo_HandlerSource_Natural), and any write to a
table with one needs SET QUOTED_IDENTIFIER ON or the insert fails with error 1934 naming indexed views.

CONVENTIONS THIS FILE FOLLOWS, ALL OF THEM LOAD-BEARING:

  * Every fixture row uses an MDPROBE0504% HandlerId, so the reset and the cleanup can find them without touching a
    real handler.
  * SOFT DELETE ONLY. There is no hard delete anywhere in this database, so cleanup sets IsDeleted = 1 and the fixture
    rows stay. The reset at the top retires anything a previous run left visible, which is what makes this file
    re-runnable.
  * REFUSALS use plain EXEC and successes use INSERT ... EXEC. That is not stylistic: INSERT ... EXEC opens a
    transaction, and a procedure that throws inside one leaves the transaction doomed (error 3930), so the CATCH cannot
    write its log row and the [R15] assertions below would measure nothing. See section L.
  * INSERT ... EXEC IS ITSELF AN ASSERTION. #Page names all 23 columns in order, so a change to the projection's column
    list, order, or types fails the insert rather than passing silently. It also succeeds on an EMPTY result set and
    fails on a MISSING one, which a row count cannot tell apart.
  * ORDER is asserted with STRING_AGG over Ordinal against a hand-computed expected string. Because every fixture row
    of the subject handler shares its HandlerId, the label is SourceType || Sequence -- unique per row within one
    handler -- and NOT the HandlerId that 503's probe could use.
  * THE FIXTURE IS INSERTED ONE ROW PER STATEMENT, not as one multi-row VALUES list. HandlerSourceId is an IDENTITY and
    the ORDER BY tiebreaker is HandlerSourceId ASCENDING, so the expected order strings below depend on identity values
    being assigned in the listed order. A single multi-row insert does that in practice and guarantees nothing.

WHAT THE FIXTURE IS. Three handlers, because @HandlerId is REQUIRED and so isolation is the first thing to check:

  HANDLER A -- MDPROBE05041, the subject. Six visible versions, listed in insertion order, which is also
  HandlerSourceId order:

  Label  Src Seq  CurrentRecord  HandlerName     Received    SrcUpdated  SortOrder
  A1     A   1    0              OLD NAME CO     2023-01-10  2026-01-05  30
  A2     A   2    0              OLD NAME CO     2023-06-15  2026-02-05  30
  A3     A   3    1              NEW NAME LLC    2024-02-20  2026-03-05  30
  B1     B   1    0              OLD NAME CO     2023-01-10  2026-04-05  20
  B2     B   2    1              NEW NAME LLC    2025-07-04  2026-05-05  20
  C1     C   1    0              ZEBRA INTERIM   2024-11-11  2026-06-05  NULL

  A1 and B1 SHARE A ReceivedDate, which is what makes the tiebreaker assertions bite: A1 precedes B1 in the ascending
  sort AND in the descending one, because the tiebreaker stays ascending when the sort reverses. Sections F1 and F2
  together are that proof -- F1 ends `A1,B1` and F2 begins `A1,B1`.
  The name changes at A3 and again at B2, which is what makes HandlerName worth offering as a sort at all.
  C1 carries a NULL SourceTypeSortOrder, the case the SourceType sort has to order deterministically.
  A3 AND B2 ARE BOTH CurrentRecord = 1. That may be legitimate -- one current version per source type -- or it may be
  the AR4 stale-flag defect. THIS PROBE ASSERTS ONLY THAT BOTH ARE VISIBLE, because a read must not decide that data is
  wrong; dbo.uspReconcileCurrentRecord owns the invariant. Section E3.

  HANDLER B -- MDPROBE05042, the NEVER-STAMPED handler. Two visible versions, CurrentRecord NULL on BOTH. This is the
  fixture for the claim 504's header makes: `CurrentRecord = 1` excludes NULL, so this handler is INVISIBLE to
  dbo.uspGetHandlerSourcePage's grid and its versions are reachable only here. Section E2 asserts both halves -- 504
  returns its rows AND dbo.vwHandlerSource returns none -- so the claim is measured rather than asserted in prose.

  HANDLER C -- MDPROBE05043. One visible version and one SOFT-DELETED version, so the exclusion and its effect on
  TotalRows can be asserted separately from everything else. Section D2.

ActivityLocation is 'MD' on every row. dbo.HandlerSource holds soft-deleted probe leftovers from earlier scripts on this
workstation and nothing visible, so every total asserted below is the fixture's own -- but section B5 cross-checks the
subject's total against dbo.vwHandlerSourceHistory rather than trusting the constant 6.

WHAT THIS PROBE CANNOT ASSERT, STATED HERE BECAUSE IT MATTERS TO MDE's REQUIREMENT. Section A0 calls the procedure with
NO arguments at all. That fails with error 201 before the procedure body executes, so the TRY/CATCH inside the
procedure never runs and NOTHING IS LOGGED. It is the one refusal this procedure structurally cannot record, and A0
asserts exactly that rather than pretending otherwise.
***********************************************************************************************************************/

SET NOCOUNT ON;
SET XACT_ABORT OFF;   -- the refusal sections need the batch to continue after a caught error
GO

PRINT N'=== da4_gethandlersourcehistorypage: dbo.uspGetHandlerSourceHistoryPage ===';
GO

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Reset. Retire anything a previous run left visible. Soft delete only.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
UPDATE dbo.HandlerSource
   SET IsDeleted             = 1
     , auditDeletedBy        = ORIGINAL_LOGIN ()
     , auditDeletedDateUtc   = SYSUTCDATETIME ()
     , auditModifiedBy       = ORIGINAL_LOGIN ()
     , auditModifiedDateUtc  = SYSUTCDATETIME ()
 WHERE HandlerId LIKE N'MDPROBE0504%'
   AND IsDeleted = 0;
PRINT CONCAT (N'reset: retired ', @@ROWCOUNT, N' leftover fixture row(s).');
GO

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Fixture. ONE STATEMENT PER ROW -- see the header: the expected order strings depend on IDENTITY being assigned in
-- this order, and a multi-row VALUES list does not promise that.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
